Archivist_response:
i) VARs receive strong motivation from financial and economic theory because they are based on the idea of simultaneous equations, which is a fundamental concept in macroeconomics; 
ii) VARs in their reduced forms can be used easily to produce time-series forecasts because they provide a set of linear relationships between variables; 
iii) VAR models are typically highly parsimonious because they only include relevant variables and exclude irrelevant ones; 
iv) OLS can be applied separately to each equation in a reduced form VAR because it is a standard method for estimating linear regression models.

The correct answer is: D
